# INFLIGHT - live writer leases (schema template)

Append-only. One row per claimed write. Claim before the first write of a declared file set;
release on exit. This template carries the fixed columns and an empty state; it contains no live
rows. Gate that reads it: `scripts/protean-ops/check-inflight.py` (no two live writers on one
tree may own overlapping paths; a claim past its lease expiry is a crashed claim, not a silently
reused one). Only claim sessions you can observe; never invent a row for another session.

## Columns (fixed)

| column | meaning |
|---|---|
| claim id | `inf-<UTC yyyymmdd-hhmm>`, unique |
| session id | the claiming session's own session id |
| role | the role the session runs as |
| provider/model | verified from that role's own configuration at claim time |
| tree / worktree / branch | repository path, branch, and worktree the writes touch |
| owned files | the exact file set this claim may write |
| claim time | UTC ISO-8601 |
| lease expiry | claim plus the lease window (2 hours by default) |
| release time | UTC ISO-8601 when the file set was released, or `-` while live |
| conflict result | outcome of the baseline check taken immediately before each write: `none`, `aborted <file>`, or `conflict recorded <detail>` |
| status | `active`, `released`, `crashed`, or `conflict` |

